    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d846">

                <pb facs="0799" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/718: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-08T15:00:00+00:00">December 8, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>215. Embassy’s 163, October 28, 10 a.m. Foreign Office informs me that agreements
                    with Great Britain and France relating to the contraband control will probably
                    be signed next week.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d846-f1"/> It will be <pb facs="0800"
                        n="788" xml:id="pg788"/> necessary, however, to make separate arrangements
                    with respect to certain articles such as nonferrous metals concerning which it
                    has not been possible to reach a satisfactory understanding. It is understood
                    that these arrangements will be similar in principle to the agreement relating
                    to the import of French iron ore and the export of coal and coke from Belgium.
                    (See Embassy’s despatch No. 528, November 22.)<anchor n="69" xml:id="d846-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Embassy’s telegram No. 202, November 28, noon.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d846-f3"/>
                    No answer has yet been received from Great Britain to the Belgian note
                    protesting against British control of exports from Belgium.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d846-f1" n="68" xml:id="d846-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 216, December 12, 4 p.m., the Chargé reported that he had been
                    reliably informed that the agreements were signed on December 11, 1939
                    (740.00112 European War 1939/756).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d846-f2" n="69" xml:id="d846-f2-content">
